From ba3029d9c01f6a0b1d9e18197ec241bbdf843ade Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 19:45:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] kv-cache: save the exact KV rotation with the state, reject a
 mismatched restore

The KV state carried no rotation metadata, so a sequence saved with Hadamard rotation (or one K tile size)
restored silently into a context with another and read back garbage keys/values. The cache now resolves the
rotation tile sizes once in the constructor (n_rot_k / n_rot_v, 0 = off), writes them with the state and refuses
a restore whose sizes differ. LLAMA_SESSION_VERSION 10 -> 11, LLAMA_STATE_SEQ_VERSION 3 -> 4: older session and
slot files are refused by the existing version check. In-process checkpoints (host and our device checkpoints)
go through the same io path and carry the 8 extra bytes per stream.

Ours kept (conflicts resolved by hand): the default-off rotation policy with LLAMA_ATTN_ROT_{K,V}_OVERRIDE and the
LLAMA_ATTN_ROT_DISABLE lock-out; the K tile env LLAMA_ATTN_ROT_K_NROT (default 64, 0 = upstream's largest power of
2) now resolves in the constructor instead of build_input_k_rot, so the saved n_rot_k is the tile the graph uses -
our tree was more exposed than upstream, because that env changed the tile between save and restore with no
record. The kv_mean_center bias-basis check reads n_rot_k != 0. Our DSA rotation list is kept as it is
(LLM_ARCH_GLM_DSA is absent from it on 88081ccb8c while b11178 had it; separate row, see REPORT/QUESTIONS).

Taken-from: ggml-org/llama.cpp@210791069b (#28498)
Measured-effect: CORRECTNESS ONLY, SPEED UNMEASURED - not yet measured; check = test-save-load-state column "rot" RED on 88081ccb8c (mismatched restores accepted), GREEN here (rejected), on a test-llama-archs llama model (head_k 128).
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
